# The dev watcher follows Cargo path dependencies, and `cms-app` depends on `cms = { path = ".." }`,
# so it watches all of apps/cms rather than just src-tauri. The frontend sources live in that same
# directory, so every edit to a .ts, .css or .html file triggered a cargo rebuild and an app
# restart -- which then threw away the Vite hot update that had already applied. Vite owns these
# files; nothing under here changes a byte of the Rust binary.
#
# This file belongs beside the crate the watcher is following, not in src-tauri. Patterns are
# gitignore syntax resolved against the directory holding the file, so a copy in src-tauri reads
# `client/` as `src-tauri/client/` and silently matches nothing -- measured: the app still
# restarted. See spec/toolchain.md.
client/
index.html
package.json
vite.config.ts
node_modules/
dist/
